WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:04.440
All right.

00:04.440 --> 00:07.640
So so far what we have done, we have prepared all the layers.

00:07.640 --> 00:11.520
So we have the setup is ready to be used in any table.

00:11.520 --> 00:15.520
So we have the functions the files, the file groups and scheme and everything is ready.

00:15.800 --> 00:17.720
But still we are not using it.

00:17.720 --> 00:20.480
The logic just exists and the files are empty.

00:20.480 --> 00:24.760
So now what we're going to do, we're going to go and create a table but not a normal one a partition

00:24.760 --> 00:25.400
table.

00:25.400 --> 00:26.440
So let's go and do that.

00:26.440 --> 00:27.560
It's very simple as well.

00:27.560 --> 00:30.480
So create table and we have to give it a name.

00:30.480 --> 00:34.040
So let's get it as well in the schema sales orders.

00:34.080 --> 00:36.280
And I'm just going to give it the name partitions.

00:36.520 --> 00:39.880
So now we have just to define like few columns inside this table.

00:40.160 --> 00:44.400
So let's get an order ID and data type int.

00:44.400 --> 00:46.560
And let's go and get an order date.

00:46.760 --> 00:49.440
We call it dates with the data type dates.

00:49.640 --> 00:53.240
And maybe just one more called sales and the data type int.

00:53.240 --> 00:56.520
So this is very normal table that we create in databases.

00:56.520 --> 00:58.560
But it's still not yet partitioned.

00:58.600 --> 01:03.120
Now in order to use everything that we have defined we're going to go do the following.

01:03.160 --> 01:04.560
We're going to say on.

01:04.600 --> 01:09.070
And now we have to tell SQL only the name of the partition scheme.

01:09.070 --> 01:12.670
So everything else is like connected a map together.

01:12.670 --> 01:15.990
Because the scheme is mapping the function with the file groups.

01:15.990 --> 01:20.070
The file groups are mapped to the data files and everything is like connected together.

01:20.070 --> 01:23.430
And here in the table we have just to give the name of the scheme.

01:23.430 --> 01:28.950
So the name of the partition scheme is scheme partition by year.

01:29.550 --> 01:32.910
And now it's very important to give a column.

01:32.910 --> 01:38.310
And since the whole logic and the function is based on a date, we cannot go and specify here for example

01:38.310 --> 01:40.790
the order ID or sales because it makes no sense.

01:40.790 --> 01:43.830
We're going to go and pick the order date and put it over here.

01:43.830 --> 01:46.230
And with that we have created a partition table.

01:46.230 --> 01:50.030
So now what we're going to do we're going to go and start inserting data to our table.

01:50.030 --> 01:50.910
So let's go and do that.

01:50.910 --> 01:56.270
So we're going to say insert into sales order partitioned.

01:57.430 --> 01:59.630
And we're going to pick values like this.

01:59.630 --> 02:00.870
So one.

02:00.910 --> 02:03.670
And then let's get any date like 2023.

02:03.790 --> 02:06.070
Like for example my the middle of the month.

02:06.070 --> 02:09.550
And the sales could be anything like let's say 100.

02:09.870 --> 02:14.030
So let's go and execute this and let's go query our table.

02:15.630 --> 02:18.190
So it is this one over here.

02:19.790 --> 02:23.030
All right, so now we have one record inside our partition table.

02:23.070 --> 02:29.190
And now the big question is in which partition in which data file did SQL store this record.

02:29.230 --> 02:31.630
So we have to test whether everything is working fine.

02:31.670 --> 02:34.670
So in order to do that I have prepared as well a query.

02:34.790 --> 02:39.950
So we are again asking the table partitions with that destination data spaces where we're going to get

02:39.950 --> 02:41.670
the number of rows in each partition.

02:41.670 --> 02:43.110
And then we have the file group.

02:43.110 --> 02:46.390
And we are focusing on our table orders partitions.

02:46.430 --> 02:48.190
So let's go and execute this one.

02:48.190 --> 02:50.990
And now we can see very easily we have the four partitions.

02:51.030 --> 02:56.510
Our new record is inserted in the correct place in 2023 file group.

02:56.550 --> 02:58.230
And in that correct partition.

02:58.230 --> 03:03.910
So with that we make sure our function and the whole logic that we have built is working correctly.

03:03.910 --> 03:06.110
So now let's go and add more records.

03:06.110 --> 03:07.870
I'm just going to go and duplicate it.

03:07.910 --> 03:09.070
Record number two.

03:09.270 --> 03:12.830
And I'm just going to pick a date in 2024.

03:13.190 --> 03:16.110
And this one going to be like 20.

03:16.310 --> 03:17.790
It just changed the value.

03:17.790 --> 03:20.310
So 50 let's go and execute it.

03:21.150 --> 03:23.980
And now we have a second row inside our table.

03:23.980 --> 03:27.020
And again the big question is whether it is working.

03:27.020 --> 03:29.100
So let's go and execute this again.

03:29.140 --> 03:36.460
And now we can see our record is inserted in the partition two in the file group 2024 which is correct.

03:36.500 --> 03:40.180
Now let's go and check the boundaries whether it is working correctly.

03:40.580 --> 03:47.100
So I'm going to go and here and the third row I'm going to say the last day of 2025.

03:47.100 --> 03:52.060
So it's going to be month 12 and the last day so 20.

03:52.500 --> 03:55.740
Let's go and insert it and check our table.

03:55.740 --> 03:57.540
So we have a new record.

03:57.580 --> 04:04.220
And now let's go and check my expectation here that this row is going to be inserted in the file group

04:04.260 --> 04:05.420
2025.

04:05.940 --> 04:07.580
So let's go and execute.

04:07.580 --> 04:08.620
And that is correct.

04:08.620 --> 04:12.500
As you can see the record is inserted in the correct partition.

04:12.500 --> 04:16.980
And this is really important to test the boundaries whether they are working correctly because it's

04:16.980 --> 04:17.820
a little bit tricky.

04:17.860 --> 04:21.060
You have this range left right and boundaries and so on.

04:21.060 --> 04:25.580
So you can do it like this to check whether the expectation of your logic is working correctly.

04:25.580 --> 04:28.100
And the last one I'm just going to do it very fast.

04:28.100 --> 04:29.410
So let's do it.

04:29.450 --> 04:32.730
2026 and I'm going to pick the first day of this year.

04:35.490 --> 04:37.170
So let's go and insert it.

04:37.250 --> 04:40.330
And now what is the expectation I think it is pretty simple.

04:40.330 --> 04:41.490
So let's go and query.

04:41.490 --> 04:45.090
And the first day of this year is inserted in the partition number four.

04:45.130 --> 04:47.250
So I can say everything is working correctly.

04:47.250 --> 04:53.210
If you got it like this then you have created successfully a partition table and you have prepared all

04:53.250 --> 04:55.890
the layers of this partition correctly.

04:55.890 --> 05:00.570
I know this is a lot of work, but to be honest, it is fun because for the first time in database you

05:00.570 --> 05:02.450
feel like you are controlling stuff.

05:02.490 --> 05:07.370
Usually in database everything like behind the scenes and you don't know exactly where the files are

05:07.370 --> 05:09.090
stored of your tables and so on.

05:09.490 --> 05:15.170
There is a lot of abstraction in databases, but here, like we are getting deep in databases and we

05:15.210 --> 05:20.650
are controlling and managing all those files, which is sometimes is nice to have this freedom and flexibility.

05:20.690 --> 05:21.090
All right.

05:21.090 --> 05:25.890
One quick thing that I would like to show you that if you go to the database in the explorer, then

05:25.890 --> 05:27.810
let's go to the storage over here.

05:27.810 --> 05:29.010
So let's expand it.

05:29.010 --> 05:31.850
And here you can find easily informations about the partitions.

05:31.850 --> 05:34.370
So over here we can find our partition scheme.

05:34.370 --> 05:37.010
And as well the partition function that we have created.

05:37.010 --> 05:39.170
It is just a quick access instead of like.

05:39.210 --> 05:40.610
Querying the metadata.

05:44.530 --> 05:47.530
So now let's have a quick summarize how everything is connected together.

05:47.570 --> 05:48.810
So we have a table.

05:48.810 --> 05:52.890
And then we specify for SQL that is connected to a partition scheme.

05:52.890 --> 05:55.410
And in the partition scheme we have everything connected.

05:55.410 --> 05:58.530
It is linked to a specific partition function.

05:58.530 --> 06:00.250
And there we have the partitions.

06:00.490 --> 06:04.330
And at the same time it is connected to file groups.

06:04.330 --> 06:07.210
And the file groups are connected to the data files.

06:07.210 --> 06:11.050
So as you can see all those layers and elements are connected together.

06:11.090 --> 06:12.250
Now let's see how this works.

06:12.250 --> 06:15.130
So we have inserted the last day of 2025.

06:15.170 --> 06:19.650
And now the first thing that's going to happen the partition function going to decide to which partition

06:19.650 --> 06:20.450
it belongs.

06:20.450 --> 06:22.890
So as you can see it is a boundary value.

06:23.010 --> 06:28.250
And since we have defined it as a lift, it's going to target the lift partition the partition three.

06:28.290 --> 06:32.090
And then the partition scheme can connect it to the right file group.

06:32.090 --> 06:35.130
And in this scenario it's going to be the file group 2025.

06:35.170 --> 06:36.530
And we have here only one file.

06:36.530 --> 06:39.410
So it can as well go to the correct data file.

06:39.410 --> 06:42.650
And in this file the SQL can store this row.

06:42.650 --> 06:44.090
So it is pretty easy.
